82: **The comment disagreement is settled by the text.** The generator explicitly says "them," referring to the 24 slots. The gate instead says the **table** is indexed unchecked, followed by singular "calls the slot" and "installs it." Grok's claim that both comments say "them" is inaccurate. Compare [generator:254](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/generate_m88k_loadstore.c:254) with [staged gate:75](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/m88kscaledbyte/table1_20261022/staged/gate_offline.sh:75). GLM's distinction is supported; "two readers" does not overturn it.
83: 
84: The source establishes twelve sync decoder consumers and four plain nosync xmem consumers. The remaining eight are `424, 440, 480, 484, 488, 496, 500, 504`. The relevant indexing and upstream rejection appear at [cpu_m88k_instr.c:2377](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:2377), [2411](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:2411), and [3606](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:3606). All 24 remain floor cells because the generator emits them.
