GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/m88kscaledbyte/pass3_20261023/grok_t1p3.txt:25:Endianness is not a free bit I invented. `m88k_cpu_new` sets big (`cpu_m88k.c:130`). `m88k_stcr` aborts a PSR byte-order flip and does not change `cpu->byte_order` (`cpu_m88k.c:523-532`). The parser's `byte_order` word sets little or big for any machine (`emul_parse.c:493-499`), and `emul.c:737-743` writes that onto the CPU. An `ELFDATA2LSB` load does the same at `file_elf.c:693-694` via `emul.c:651-652`. Both endiannesses are in the producer's image, so the decoder installs twelve slots and `xmem_slow` calls four.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/m88kscaledbyte/pass3_20261023/grok_t1p3.txt:27:`xmem_slow`'s `user` is `iword & 0x80` (`:2359`). The register-form decoder treats that same bit as `.wt` and `goto bad` before installing `xmem_slow` (`:3606-3614`). Immediate xmem is only op26 0x00 and 0x01, so bits 31-28 are clear, `regofs` is 0, and `:2368-2372` forces `scaled = 0` and `user = 0`. The only `m88k_loadstore[` sites are `:2377`, `:2411`, `:3087`, and `:3622`. Immediate `:3087` adds neither scaledness, usr, register-offset, nor no-pc-sync, so its range stops at 31. Register xmem reaches a byte only for bits 11-10 = 00 (bit 10 clear → size component 0); bits 11-10 = 01 is a word; 10 and 11 are rejected before the call. Signedness is absent from both xmem indices. The eight leftover slots have no caller. The new generator sentence (`generate_m88k_loadstore.c:259-263`) matches that image. The gate comment stays singular, as F9 required (`gate_offline.sh:189-191`).
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/m88kscaledbyte/pass3_20261023/grok_t1p3.txt:29:R1: the block is at `gate_offline.sh:187-232`, after `CC=$(command -v cc || command -v gcc)` (`:185`) and before `need_file` (`:234`). The call is `GEN= TABLE= CC="$CC"`. `staged/insert_HEAD.diff` is the one hunk. R2 is `diff_m88k_loadstore_gen.sh:95`: `command -v cc` succeeds → `cc`, otherwise `gcc`. `driver_r1.diff` is only F25, the CC header, that default, and the sum formula. R3 is comment-only; `TABLE_UNCHANGED.out` gives both md5s as `d222e737a0644e3b633fc1bffdb8e974`.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/m88kscaledbyte/pass3_20261023/grok_t1p3.txt:33:Each of the 54 spec indices is checked by absolute name in both artifacts (`diff_m88k_loadstore_gen.sh:217-224`). A renamed contracted cell fails that row when both artifacts change; a one-sided change also fails `cmp_fresh_committed`. The 185/186 swap is outside the spec: `F25.out` records 1/123 red when only the table changes and 0/123 when both change. Handler bodies are outside this contract (driver header, NOT OBSERVED). The move adds `CC="$CC"` and the placement sentence; the pin, accept, and counterpart lists are the same strings. Success-path gate checks are 3 summary + 123 identity = 126, and `GATE2_committedform_tail.out` contains 126 lines matching `ok   m88k loadstore generator:`.
