## Q1 -- the diff, checked against the producers

Read `GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c` (line numbers match this tree), `generate_m88k_loadstore.c`, `regress/diff_m88k_loadstore_gen.sh`, and `regress/gate_offline.sh`. Flag values at `generate_m88k_loadstore.c:46-52` and `cpu_m88k_instr.c:298-304` are store 4, signedness 8, endianness 16, scaledness 32, usr 64, register-offset 128, no-pc-sync 256. The printer loops (`generate_m88k_loadstore.c:221-234`) step by those values, size 0..3 innermost, so the slot number is the sum of the loop variables. The old weighted boolean formula is gone.

The 24 repaired slots are exactly register-offset + scaled + size 0, over the flag combinations the generator does not NULL. Walked:

| Slot | Sum | Who emits it |
|---|---|---|
| 160, 176, 224, 240 | 128+32, +16, +64, +64+16 | Decoder unsigned byte load. `(iword & 0xf800) == 0x800` and bit 10 set forces `opsize = 0`, `signedness = 0` (`cpu_m88k_instr.c:3592-3597`). User is bit 0x100. Endian is `cpu->byte_order`. |
| 168, 184, 232, 248 | those + 8 | Decoder signed byte load. Bits 15-12 = 0x1 and bits 11-10 = 11 leave `signedness` at 1 (`:3599-3600` does not clear it). |
| 164, 180, 228, 244 | store +4 on the unsigned pairs | Decoder store. Bits 15-12 = 0x2, bits 11-10 = 11, `op == 1` forces `signedness = 0`. |
| 416, 420, 432, 436 | 256+128+32, +4, +16, +16+4 | `xmem_slow` load and store. |
| 424, 440, 480, 484, 488, 496, 500, 504 | signed and/or usr on the nosync base | No assignment reaches these. |

That is 12 + 4 + 8.

Endianness is not a free bit I invented. `m88k_cpu_new` sets big (`cpu_m88k.c:130`). `m88k_stcr` aborts a PSR byte-order flip and does not change `cpu->byte_order` (`cpu_m88k.c:523-532`). The parser's `byte_order` word sets little or big for any machine (`emul_parse.c:493-499`), and `emul.c:737-743` writes that onto the CPU. An `ELFDATA2LSB` load does the same at `file_elf.c:693-694` via `emul.c:651-652`. Both endiannesses are in the producer's image, so the decoder installs twelve slots and `xmem_slow` calls four.

`xmem_slow`'s `user` is `iword & 0x80` (`:2359`). The register-form decoder treats that same bit as `.wt` and `goto bad` before installing `xmem_slow` (`:3606-3614`). Immediate xmem is only op26 0x00 and 0x01, so bits 31-28 are clear, `regofs` is 0, and `:2368-2372` forces `scaled = 0` and `user = 0`. The only `m88k_loadstore[` sites are `:2377`, `:2411`, `:3087`, and `:3622`. Immediate `:3087` adds neither scaledness, usr, register-offset, nor no-pc-sync, so its range stops at 31. Register xmem reaches a byte only for bits 11-10 = 00 (bit 10 clear  size component 0); bits 11-10 = 01 is a word; 10 and 11 are rejected before the call. Signedness is absent from both xmem indices. The eight leftover slots have no caller. The new generator sentence (`generate_m88k_loadstore.c:259-263`) matches that image. The gate comment stays singular, as F9 required (`gate_offline.sh:189-191`).

R1: the block is at `gate_offline.sh:187-232`, after `CC=$(command -v cc || command -v gcc)` (`:185`) and before `need_file` (`:234`). The call is `GEN= TABLE= CC="$CC"`. `staged/insert_HEAD.diff` is the one hunk. R2 is `diff_m88k_loadstore_gen.sh:95`: `command -v cc` succeeds  `cc`, otherwise `gcc`. `driver_r1.diff` is only F25, the CC header, that default, and the sum formula. R3 is comment-only; `TABLE_UNCHANGED.out` gives both md5s as `d222e737a0644e3b633fc1bffdb8e974`.

